codex
I’ve settled the contract shape: each node may persist an `on_error` object with `policy` plus bounded retry parameters. Retry remains limited by the existing `retry` capability; explicit error routing and optional skipping get their own registry capability flags. Failures will carry the full stable structured payload in records and SSE events, while error edges themselves carry only a control token.
